  "findings": [
    "The original primary valid inputs now match. New cross-mechanism controls exercise the changed consumers on at least two independent axes; linked valid failures remain binding to whole-source closure. This does not imply every isolated equation is wrong.",
    "Four active grouped external border/direction cases match. Parallel message ownership loses the message/activation (35 versus30 elements). Create/run/destroy differs in lifeline start and canvas height218px Java versus228px Rust. All four initial order/create matrix inputs are Java-negative because deactivate/activate are attached to the same message; Rust accepts all four. They are retained as rejection evidence, never valid history passes. Port message-parallel identity, CREATE and standalone DESTROY tiles and Java input validation; valid coverage comes from the six remaining probes.",
    "Five depth/group-note/delay callback controls match, supporting the ordinary three-pass traversal and staircase repair. Standalone destruction after a group then a self arrow fails: Java266px versus248px, the missing18px cross tile propagates to subsequent events and lifelines. Callback replay cannot be accepted separately from the scheduler that supplies its y values. Preserve lifecycle state across measurement/background, with creation and destroy metadata, rather than adding a fitted final offset.",
    "Historic review.json and every retained input/reference are unchanged. New record describes candidate0fb4e14b only. Cross-linked sources are counted once in the68-case fresh matrix, not copied into additional directories."
  ],
  "verdict": "rejected"
}
